crates/workspace: the multi-workspace state is written on quit.

`MultiWorkspace::flush_serialization` wrapped its write in a foreground task.
`App::shutdown` waits for the quit handlers by blocking the main thread, so
the task never ran. Every quit logged "timed out waiting on app_will_quit"
after 200 ms and exited without the write. Not MikuOS's: gpui's scheduler
blocks the same way everywhere. Found by timing each quit handler.

--- a/crates/workspace/src/multi_workspace.rs
+++ b/crates/workspace/src/multi_workspace.rs
@@ -1474,10 +1474,14 @@
 
     /// Used by the quit handler to ensure pending DB writes
     /// complete before the process exits.
+    ///
+    /// On a background thread: the quit handler's futures are waited on by
+    /// blocking the main thread (`App::shutdown`), so a foreground task here
+    /// never ran, and every quit timed out waiting on it with the write lost.
     pub fn flush_serialization(&mut self, cx: &mut Context<Self>) -> Task<()> {
         self._serialize_task.take();
         let serialization = self.serialize_now(cx);
-        cx.spawn(async move |_, _| serialization.await)
+        cx.background_spawn(serialization)
     }
 
